@page "/mcp"

<DocPage Href="mcp" Title="MCP server"
         Lead="This site hosts a Model Context Protocol server, so an AI agent can work against Blex's real API, docs and generator instead of guessing at them.">

    <p>
        Point an MCP client at <code>https://blex.bitplatform.dev/mcp</code> - or at
        <code>http://localhost:5280/mcp</code> when you run the documentation site locally. It speaks the
        streamable HTTP transport, needs no authentication, and every tool on it is read-only.
    </p>

    <CodeBlock Code="@ClaudeCode" Language="bash" Title="Claude Code" />
    <CodeBlock Code="@VsCode" Language="json" FileName=".vscode/mcp.json" />

    <h2>Tools</h2>
    <p>
        One rule holds across the reference tools: pass the key of the thing you want and you get that thing;
        leave it out and you get the index of what there is. Every tool is also a plain HTTP GET under
        <code>/api/mcp/...</code> - <a href="api/mcp/GetBlexApi" target="_blank" rel="noopener">/api/mcp/GetBlexApi</a> is the type list -
        so you can look at any answer in a browser.
    </p>
    <ApiTable Rows="@Tools" MemberHeader="Tool" />

    <h2>InspectBlexStore</h2>
    <p>
        The one question documentation cannot answer is "what does the generator do with <em>this</em> class?".
        <code>InspectBlexStore</code> answers it by running the real <code>Bit.Blex.Generators</code> over the
        source it is given. It returns every <code>BLEX</code> diagnostic a build would report, the compiler
        errors in the result, and the exact public members the generator adds - so an agent calls
        <code>Increment()</code> because the generator said so, not because it guessed the naming convention.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock Code="@InspectRequest" Language="bash" Title="Try it from a terminal" />

    <h2>Resources and prompts</h2>
    <ApiTable Rows="@Resources" MemberHeader="Resource" />
    <ApiTable Rows="@Prompts" MemberHeader="Prompt" />

    <p>
        The server also hands the model a short set of working rules at <code>initialize</code>, before any tool
        is called, and completes every argument that is a key into a closed set - the docs slugs, the guide
        headings, the type names, the diagnostic ids and the source paths.
    </p>

</DocPage>

@code {
    private static readonly IReadOnlyList<ApiTable.Row> Tools =
    [
        new("SearchBlex", "Searches the guide, the docs pages, every public member, the generator's diagnostics and the demo's sources at once; every hit names the follow-up call that returns its full text."),
        new("GetBlexSetupGuide", "The wiring for one hosting model - <code>server</code>, <code>wasm</code>, <code>auto</code>, <code>standalone-wasm</code>, <code>maui-hybrid</code> or <code>maui</code> - as the real files of a working project."),
        new("GetBlexGuideSection", "One section of the reference guide (the README) as Markdown."),
        new("GetBlexDocsPage", "One page of this site as Markdown, rendered by the same component you are reading."),
        new("GetBlexApi", "One public type in full - every member with its type, its real default value and its documentation - read out of the shipped assemblies."),
        new("GetBlexDiagnostics", "One <code>BLEX</code> diagnostic with its cause, a rejected store and the fix."),
        new("InspectBlexStore", "Runs the real generator over store source and returns its diagnostics and the members it generates."),
        new("GetBlexSourceFile", "One source file of this site or of the standalone sample, verbatim."),
    ];

    private static readonly IReadOnlyList<ApiTable.Row> Resources =
    [
        new("blex://guide, blex://guide/{heading}", "The reference guide, whole or by section."),
        new("blex://docs/{slug}", "A documentation page. Every page is also listed as a concrete resource."),
        new("blex://api, blex://api/{typeName}", "The type index, or one type in full."),
        new("blex://diagnostics, blex://diagnostics/{code}", "The diagnostics table, or one diagnostic in full."),
        new("blex://source/{path}", "A source file of the demo or the sample."),
    ];

    private static readonly IReadOnlyList<ApiTable.Row> Prompts =
    [
        new("add-blex-to-app", "Adds Blex to an existing app, in the right order for its hosting model."),
        new("implement-blex-feature", "Builds a state feature with the real API, checking every store with the generator."),
        new("migrate-to-blex", "Moves an app off Fluxor (or hand-rolled state services) one feature at a time."),
        new("debug-blex-state", "Diagnoses a component that does not re-render, lost persisted state, BLEX build errors and the like."),
    ];

    private const string ClaudeCode = """
        claude mcp add --transport http bit-blex https://blex.bitplatform.dev/mcp
        """;

    private const string VsCode = """
        {
          "servers": {
            "bit-blex": {
              "type": "http",
              "url": "https://blex.bitplatform.dev/mcp"
            }
          }
        }
        """;

    private const string InspectRequest = """
        curl -G "https://blex.bitplatform.dev/api/mcp/InspectBlexStore" \
          --data-urlencode "source=[BlexStore] public partial class CounterStore { [BlexState] private int _count; [BlexAction] private void OnIncrement() => Count++; }"
        """;
}
